# Condition 5 of BACKEND-PLAN.md §0.3.1: api/app/security/ is a protected path so that
# changes there get a deliberate second read rather than a drive-by edit. Working solo,
# the value is the forced pause, not the second person.
#
# Owner set to @Rymerpop03 when the repository was first pushed to GitHub. A CODEOWNERS
# file naming an account that does not exist silently protects nothing — GitHub assigns
# nobody and the review rule never fires — so `api/tools/check_codeowners.py` runs in CI
# and fails if a placeholder ever comes back.
#
# Required by BACKEND-PLAN.md §0.3.1 condition 5, which is why the security paths below
# are listed individually rather than relying on the catch-all.

*                           @Rymerpop03

